# start Validation Reply Form
_vrf_PLAT242_(S2MeBA)2PbI4_298K
;
PROBLEM: Low    'MainMol' Ueq as Compared to Neighbors of         C9 Check
RESPONSE: Due to the thermal motion of the carbon atom at room temperature, it is not ideally shaped and displacement parameters are not very constant, but the atom-type assignment is correct. Notably, this problem can be avoided in the 100K structure.
;
_vrf_PLAT242_(S2MeBA)2PbI4_298K_2
;
PROBLEM: Low    'MainMol' Ueq as Compared to Neighbors of         C5 Check
RESPONSE: Due to the thermal motion of the carbon atom at room temperature, it is not ideally shaped and displacement parameters are not very constant, but the atom-type assignment is correct. Notably, this problem can be avoided in the 100K structure.
;
_vrf_PLAT412_(S2MeBA)2PbI4_298K
;
PROBLEM: Short Intra XH3 .. XHn     H7C      ..H42B     .       1.54 Ang.
RESPONSE: These hydrogen atoms belong to terminal carbons and are in calculated positions (not independently refined). The relatively stronger thermal motion of terminal carbon atoms at room temperature leads to this problem, which does not impact the overall quality of the structure solution. Notably, this problem was avoided in the 100K structure, where thermal motion is reduced.
;
_vrf_PLAT412_(S2MeBA)2PbI4_298K_2
;
PROBLEM: Short Intra XH3 .. XHn     H10C     ..H20B     .       1.61 Ang.
RESPONSE: These hydrogen atoms belong to terminal carbons and are in calculated positions (not independently refined). The relatively stronger thermal motion of terminal carbon atoms at room temperature leads to this problem, which does not impact the overall quality of the structure solution. Notably, this problem was avoided in the 100K structure, where thermal motion is reduced.
;
_vrf_PLAT213_(S2MeBA)2PbI4_298K
;
PROBLEM: Atom C4              has ADP max/min Ratio .....        4.1 prolat
RESPONSE: This problem is due to C4 atom being located in a position that was either impacted by thermal motion or disorder. Modeling of disorder was attempted but it could not be stabilized. Notably, this problem can be avoided by lowering the temperature to 100K.
;
_vrf_PLAT241_(S2MeBA)2PbI4_298K
;
PROBLEM: High   'MainMol' Ueq as Compared to Neighbors of         C6 Check
RESPONSE: Due to the thermal motion of the carbon atom at room temperature, it is not ideally shaped and displacement parameters are not very constant, but the atom-type assignment is correct. Notably, this problem can be avoided in the 100K structure.
;
