RESPONSE: Due to the thermal motion of the carbon atom at room temperature, it is not ideally shaped and displacement parameters are not very constant, but the atom-type assignment is correct. Notably, this problem can be avoided in the 100K structure.
;
_vrf_PLAT242_(S2MeBA)2PbI4_298K_3
;
PROBLEM: Low    'MainMol' Ueq as Compared to Neighbors of         C3 Check
RESPONSE: Due to the thermal motion of the carbon atom at room temperature, it is not ideally shaped and displacement parameters are not very constant, but the atom-type assignment is correct. Notably, this problem can be avoided in the 100K structure.
;
_vrf_PLAT342_(S2MeBA)2PbI4_298K
;
PROBLEM: Low Bond Precision on  C-C Bonds ...............     0.0325 Ang.
RESPONSE: This problem is due to the thermal motion of the carbon atoms at room temperature. Nevertheless, the organic cation carbon and nitrogen atom positions were unambiguously determined during the refinement.
;
_vrf_PLAT410_(S2MeBA)2PbI4_298K
;
PROBLEM: Short Intra H...H Contact  H3A      ..H6       .       1.84 Ang.
RESPONSE: H3A and H6 hydrogen atoms are in calculated positions (not independently refined). The relatively stronger thermal motion of these carbon atoms at room temperature leads to this problem, which does not impact the overall quality of the structure solution. Notably, this problem was avoided in the 100K structure, where thermal motion is reduced.
;
_vrf_PLAT412_(S2MeBA)2PbI4_298K_3
;
PROBLEM: Short Intra XH3 .. XHn     H6       ..H42A     .       1.78 Ang.
RESPONSE: H6 and H42A hydrogen atoms belong to two close carbons and are in calculated positions. The relatively stronger thermal motion of these carbon atoms at room temperature leads to this problem, which does not impact the overall quality of the structure solution. Notably, this problem was avoided in the 100K structure, where thermal motion is reduced.
;
